-- title:
--   Stopping rules of the finite-horizon problem
-- statement:
--   A **stopping rule** for the problem with $n$ stages assigns to each sample $\omega=((Y_1,U_1),\dots,(Y_n,U_n))$ of base rewards and independent uniform coins a stage $\tau(\omega)\in\{1,\dots,n\}\cup\{n+1\}$, where $n+1$ means that nothing is accepted (payoff $0$), such that for each $i\le n$ the event $\{\tau=i\}$ depends only on $(Y_1,U_1),\dots,(Y_i,U_i)$.
--
--   Because the coins are part of the observation, randomized rules are included.
--
--   **Formalization Note** Stages are numbered from $0$, so $\tau$ takes values in $\{0,\dots,n\}$ and $\tau=n$ means "never stop". Measurability is with respect to the σ-algebra generated by the coordinates $j\le i$.
-- source:
--   Kim–Perchet, Effective Horizons for Prophet Inequalities with Discounted I.I.D. Rewards, STOC 2027 submission (manuscript sha256 2ee8cccf…), Section 3, p.3; A.5, p.33

import Mathlib

namespace EffHorizonProphet.Supplement

/-- A **stopping rule** for the finite-horizon problem with `n` stages (Kim–Perchet, *Effective Horizons for Prophet Inequalities with Discounted I.I.D. Rewards*, STOC 2027
submission (manuscript sha256 2ee8cccf…), Section 3, p.3;
A.5, p.33): a stopping time with values in `{1, …, n} ∪ {n + 1}`, where `n + 1` means that no
reward is accepted.

**Formalization Note** Stages are `0`-based, so `τ ω ∈ {0, …, n}` and `τ ω = n` is "never stop"
(payoff `0`). A sample point is the sequence of stage pairs `(Y_j, U_j)` (base reward and an
independent uniform coin, as in Remark 16). The event `{τ = i}` must be measurable for the
σ-algebra generated by the pairs of stages `j ≤ i`. This filtration contains the paper's
`σ(Y_1, …, Y_i)`, so randomized rules are included. -/
def IsStoppingRule {n : ℕ} (τ : (Fin n → ℝ × unitInterval) → ℕ) : Prop :=
  (∀ ω, τ ω ≤ n) ∧
    ∀ i : Fin n,
      @MeasurableSet _ (MeasurableSpace.comap
        (fun ω : Fin n → ℝ × unitInterval => fun j : {j : Fin n // j ≤ i} => ω j)
        MeasurableSpace.pi) {ω | τ ω = i}

end EffHorizonProphet.Supplement


